  "body": "## Problem\n\nPR #1671 turns a closed STEP body that is wound inward outward at import, and says so. The STL and OBJ importers do not do this. An inward closed STL or OBJ body keeps a negative signed volume.\n\n`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/pencil.rs` and `deburr.rs` use the facet winding to tell a concave edge from a convex edge. An inward body swaps the two. Pencil can then trace convex edges, and deburr can select concave corners. No gouge path is known. The heights were not examined.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A closed, consistently wound STL or OBJ body with a negative signed volume imports turned outward, with a note in the import result and on the status line. Or the import refuses it with a clear message.\n- A pinning test for each format.\n- The trace of pencil and deburr heights for an inward body is recorded on this issue.\n\nPart of the work that #1617 started.\n",
